  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Sheng Ji. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "In Sheng Ji, your team wins rounds by controlling opponents' point-card captures while handling dynamic trump rank and suit. Bidding, kitty management, and combination play decide long-session rank progression.",
    objective: "Raise your partnership rank from 2 upward (often to Ace) by winning rounds while controlling opponents' trick points.",
    gameplay: "Each round establishes dominant rank and usually a dominant suit through bidding. Declarers take the kitty and discard back to kitty size. Trick play then proceeds with strict follow/combination constraints based on lead pattern and trump structure. Opponents' captured point cards (5s, 10s, Kings) determine whether declarers keep deal and advance or defenders seize momentum.",
    keyRules: [
      'Dynamic trump rank each round changes comparative card power.',
      'Only 5s, 10s, and Kings score points in tricks.',
      "Round control shifts based on opponents' point total thresholds.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Usually 4 players in fixed partnerships (partners sit opposite).',
      deck: 'Commonly two full decks with jokers (108 cards total).',
      equipment: 'Cards and score/rank tracking.',
      dealing: 'Players draw one card at a time during deal; in two-deck four-player games, each player gets 25 cards and 8 cards remain as kitty/bottom.',
    },
    turnFlow: "Each round establishes dominant rank and usually a dominant suit through bidding. Declarers take the kitty and discard back to kitty size. Trick play then proceeds with strict follow/combination constraints based on lead pattern and trump structure. Opponents' captured point cards (5s, 10s, Kings) determine whether declarers keep deal and advance or defenders seize momentum.",
